  "body": "The preceding tensor certificate bounded a metric coefficient and its first time derivative while leaving the complete curvature contribution unevaluated. This change derives the selected angular-screen magnetic Weyl second variation for the registered normal-t/spatial-normal-y observers, including the complete scalar quadratic, observer, radial-normal, connection and epsilon terms. On the exterior sphere `(x,r)=(1/4,5/4)`, its coefficient is enclosed in `[-0.024929793753,-0.004128493946]`; the quadratic contribution cannot cancel the linear response.\n\nThe capsule specifies the selected TT pair, orientation and great-circle zeros. It retains the parent formal-response premises and makes no gauge-invariant clock/observer, physical radiation, finite-amplitude nonlinear-family or cosmological-origin claim. The compatible full second-order boundary problem remains unfinished. Earlier research and manuscripts are frozen; the English/Spanish landing pages receive additive text only. No new Zenodo version or journal submission is made.\n\nValidation:\n\n- Exact all-sphere curl and scalar quadratic reductions; independent full five-dimensional coordinate-curvature fixtures, including `g=g0+lambda*q+lambda\u00b2*k/2`.\n- Fresh extracted and relocated ZIP replay: 26 positive runs, six exact-reason expected failures, 28 reference byte matches and 12 normal/optimized parity groups.\n- Sixteen source-integrity and three ZIP-integrity rejection controls; all ten complete input capsules unchanged before/after; standard-library runtime.\n- All 11,910 unmodified prior HDblast leaves remain exact; the three intended public-text insertions have full inverse-byte checks. The new source contains 60 files and 18 indexed Python programs.\n\nA dedicated workflow repeats the bounded replay and independently verifies the receipt. Remote CI results and publication readbacks are recorded separately after publication.\n",
